      answer: "b",
      explanation: "PTH promotes calcium reabsorption in distal nephron segments, including the DCT. It reduces rather than increases proximal phosphate reabsorption. Reducing calcium uptake or increasing its urinary loss would not conserve filtered calcium; its intestinal effect is indirect through active vitamin D.",
      sectionId: "excretion-distal-tubule", source: { document: "biology", page: 99 }, cognitive: "recall"
