      answer: "b",
      explanation: "Glucose is normally filtered and then largely reclaimed. When filtered delivery exceeds transport capacity, some remains in urine despite continued reabsorption. A renal threshold describes appreciable urinary appearance, not the onset of filtration or complete cessation of uptake.",
