      answer: "a",
      explanation: "The oblique intramural ureter is compressed as the bladder fills, producing a functional anti-reflux arrangement. This is not the voluntary external urethral sphincter. Ureteric peristalsis still propels urine; the oblique course does not replace it with passive pressure flow.",
